      "message": "dear sir,\n\nbasically, we think using existing vendor hook is reasonable,\nbut i meet some problem as below:\n1. the existing hook was from silicon vendor, such as qualcom/mtk, \n   in my optional, we can\u0027t use it beacuse it should be silicon solution.\nfor example,below is a merged change:\nANDROID: sched: Add restricted vendor hooks in CFS scheduler\n\nAdd restricted vendor hooks in CFS scheduler class to allow\ncustomizations in vendor modules.\n\nBug: 180668820\nChange-Id: I69bd90e11220d7607b075a3aa687059deaa60439\nSigned-off-by: Pavankumar Kondeti \u003cquic_pkondeti@quicinc.com\u003e\nfair.c\nexisting vendor hook:\ntrace_android_rvh_check_preempt_wakeup(rq, p, \u0026preempt);\n\tif (preempt)\n\t\tgoto preempt;\nxiaomi vendor hook:\ntrace_android_rvh_oem_check_preempt_wakeup(rq, p, wake_flags, \u0026resched);\n\tif (resched)\n\t\tgoto preempt;\n\t\t\n2. the previous hook is from oem, it should be used by us, but the function parameters are different,\n   for example:\n   \n   fair.c\n   oppo\u0027s vendor hook(merged):\n   \ttrace_android_rvh_replace_next_task_fair(rq, \u0026p, \u0026se, \u0026repick, true);\n\tif (repick)\n\t\tgoto done;\n\n    xiaomi vendor hook:\t\t\n\ttrace_android_rvh_oem_pick_next_task_fair(rq, prev, \u0026p, \u0026se, \u0026find);\n\tif (find) {\n\t\tcfs_rq \u003d cfs_rq_of(se);\n\t\tset_next_entity(cfs_rq, se);\n\t\tgoto done;\n\t}\n  so my problem is:\n   Is there any way to use one hook and same parameters?",
